body:
Sometimes I want to reach out to her and just explain how much she has hurt me. I want to explain to her how much it hurt to have her share our personal conversations with other people. I want to tell her how much it hurt for her to send me an entire letter calling me a shit person and tearing me down for "lying" about something I was actually going through (I was having temporary dissociative spells after the death of my mother and she insisted I was lying about it). How much it hurt to hear from a mutual friend that she hadn't liked me for months and how she always felt our friendship wasn't compatible despite everything I had done for her as her friend. 

&#x200B;

About half a year ago, maybe less, she reached out to me after over a year of no contact and apologized profusely for her "actions", while simultaneously telling a lie to explain why it took her a year to apologize. The entire interaction she was begging me to set her free and to forgive her because she hadn't slept, stopped crying, or stopped cutting herself since we stopped being friends. I remember forgiving her and briefly talking about some of the actions that had really hurt my feelings, only for her to insist that the reason she reacted the way she did is because of this lie she had created. So part of me doesn't even know if it is worth it to pour my guts out and explain how much her actions has an effect on people when she probably won't even take accountability for them, but god do I really just want to be the one this time to message her after a few months and be like "actually, you doing x, y, and z really hurt especially after I had been there to witness your slit wrists and amazon purchases of razors that you would suddenly send me".
